ppu/spu: read and write watch diagnostics for finding who reads a value (all off by default).
Toro's own patch (7xxx); diagnostic only: the store and load paths it changes behave as before unless PPU_RWATCH,
PPU_WWATCH_FN or SPU_DMAWATCH is set, and nothing is printed unless one of the switches below is set.
What:
- PPU_RWATCH_UNIQUE=1 (with PPU_RWATCH=<hex>[,len]) logs one line per distinct reading site, keyed on the host return
  address and the guest lr (so memcpy called from different guest callers stays apart): address, size, value, guest
  function, lr, thread; up to PPU_RWATCH_UNIQUE_MAX (default 256, max 4096); guest stack for the first 16. Unset: old
  behaviour (24 hits).
- PPU_WWATCH_FN=<hex guest fn> logs every vm_write* store made by that function (PPU_WWATCH_FN_MAX, default 64, 0 =
  unlimited), to find an object address from the function that fills it.
- PPU_RWATCH_FOLLOW=1 (with PPU_WWATCH_FN) watches the objects that function fills: a 32-bit store at A then one at
  A+0xC sets a 16-byte window at A; PPU_RWATCH_FOLLOW_VAL=<hex>[,width] follows the first store of that value instead.
  Up to 8 windows; when full, the oldest is replaced, so objects created late are still watched.
- PPU_RWATCH also sees vm_read64, the HLE _sys_memcpy/_sys_memcmp source ranges and, in a build with -DPPU_RW_HOOKS
  (needs a re-lift), the lifted code's direct loads (lvx, lvlx, lvrx, lvebx/ehx/ewx, lwbrx, lhbrx, ldbrx). Overlap
  test, so a 16-byte load covering the window is caught.
- SPU_DMAWATCH=<hexlo>-<hexhi>[,...] (up to 8 ranges) logs every SPU main-memory read that overlaps a range (mfc GET
  and GETL elements, GETLLAR, raw-SPU GET); SPU_DMAWATCH_MAX caps the lines (default 2000).
- CELLPAD_BUFLOG=1: cellPadGetData prints each distinct (port, guest buffer) once (up to 8).
Why: these found the reader of the pad sensor words in the chick minigame (func_00116BF8, latching them for the
minigame script) after the plain watch had only covered pad objects created in the menus.
